index 0000000..e4536d9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Logging lanes: archive, audit, alert
+
+Observability is split into three explicit lanes. Pick the lane first,
+then write the code. Discord is never a Monolog channel.
+
+## The three lanes
+
+| Lane | Mechanism | Where | Retention |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | `Log::debug/info/warning/error(...)` (default `stack` → `daily`) | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (rotated daily) | 14 days (`LOG_DAILY_DAYS`) |
+| **Audit** | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` | `storage/logs/audit.log` (rotated daily) | 90 days (`LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`) |
+| **Alert** | `app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send($title, $message, $context)` | Discord incoming webhook | n/a (human paging) |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+- **Archive (default):** routine application logs, debug to error. Anything
+  you would `tail` or grep after the fact. Example: `Log::warning('Asaas webhook signature mismatch', ['event' => $type])`.
+- **Audit (who changed / tried what):** durable trail of security- or
+  money-relevant state changes and denied attempts. Membership role changes,
+  subscription transitions, login lockouts, queue access grants. Always
+  include the actor, the subject, and the before/after (or the attempted
+  action). Minimum level `info`. Example:
+  `Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', ['actor_id' => $actor->id, 'from' => $from, 'to' => $to])`.
+- **Alert (wake someone up):** only for actionable ops incidents — a job that
+  exhausted its retries, a payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit
+  blocking an entity. Explicit call only:
+  `app(\App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send('Asaas webhook failing', '...', ['queue' => 'asaas-webhooks'])`.
+  If it is not worth paging about, it is archive or audit, not an alert.
+
+Rules:
+
+- Discord ≠ `Log::`. There is no `discord` log channel and there must never
+  be one. Alerting is an explicit decision in code, not a log level.
+- Never log secrets or PII beyond what the trail needs. `DiscordOpsAlert`
+  redacts sensitive context keys (`password`, `token`, `secret`,
+  `authorization`, `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`, `webhook`), any `Bearer ...`
+  credential in a string value, and nested arrays recursively — but prefer to
+  not pass secrets at all.
+- `DiscordOpsAlert` soft-fails: transport errors and non-2xx responses are
+  logged at `error` level without the webhook URL and never thrown to the
+  caller.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Key | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels behind the default `stack` (keep `daily`). |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention (days). |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Minimum level for the `audit` channel. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention (days). |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | empty (disabled) | Discord incoming webhook. When empty/unset, `DiscordOpsAlert::send()` is a silent no-op. |
+
+When `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` is not configured, alerts are silently dropped
+(no HTTP request). Production sets it; local/test leave it empty.
